{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>And you shall remember all the commandments of HaShem.</b> Rashi explained: the gematria of ציצית is 600; with 8 threads and 5 knots, that makes 613. And since the three words ציצת (in the phrase) are defective (lacking) their final yod, <b>לציצת</b> is written — the lamed completes the gematria of the three words ציצית, for each one totals 613 in gematria." "<b>And you shall not go about after your hearts and after your eyes.</b> When you see My commandments, you shall remember that you are My servants, and you shall not accustom the heart and the eye to transgress My commandments."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The text says שלשת תיבות של ציצת — literally 'the three words of ציצת,' meaning the three occurrences of the word in the tsitsit passage; kept literal as 'the three words ציצת.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:09.915569877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}